## Summary

Implemented the plan's declared UI follow-up: **Settings page → "Upgrade holds" section** for
`arch_config['ignored_packages']` (plan `docs/plans/2026-08-16-gui-upgrade-holds.md`, Status:
implemented). One commit `722c4a0` — 6 files, +183/−2:

- `atlas/view/webview/api.py` — `get_app_settings()` returns `arch.ignored_packages`;
  `save_app_settings()` accepts it (key widened to include `'ignored_packages'`), cleans
  (`sorted({n.strip() for n in held if isinstance(n, str) and n.strip()})`), persists. Only
  touched when present in the payload.
- `atlas/view/webview/main.js` — holds section (chips with remove buttons, add box with
  client-side validation `[A-Za-z0-9@._+:-]+`, Enter adds, duplicate-guard, empty state),
  rendered only when `arch.available`; `saveSettings` collects rows into
  `payload.arch.ignored_packages`.
- `atlas/view/webview/style.css` — `.settings-holds-list/-hold/-hold-add` (existing tokens).
- `tests/view/webview/test_api.py` — 3 new AppSettingsTest cases (get includes holds; save
  cleans/sorts/persists; arch save without the key leaves holds untouched).
- `tests/view/webview/main_js_contracts.test.js` — `testSettingsUpgradeHoldsRender` (chips
  render; section absent without Arch).

**Verification:** 780 Python tests + 61 JS contract tests, all green (both re-run this
session). Suite count moved 777→780, JS 60→61 — docs and skill baseline updated.

## Known gaps / next steps

- **Holds GUI not eyeballed on a real box.** Manual pass (unit + contract tested only): add
  `bazaar` in Settings → `Update all` skips it (`--ignore=bazaar`, reason "Held (ignored
  upgrade)") → remove hold in Settings → proposed again. Same holds for the vendored-conflict
  dialog (still needs a real conflict; recreate the bazaar 0.9.4-1 ↔ libdex scenario).
- **Same-pass mutual-conflict stranding** (documented known gap, deliberate + test-locked):
  a mutual pair first detected in one pass with neither side pre-scheduled strands both in
  `cannot_upgrade`. Revisit only if it bites in the wild.
- User-facing strings in all 10 locales (conflict dialog) were written by translation, not
  native speakers — worth a skim.
- `upgrade_several`'s `-dd` append (skip_dependency_checks) remains — user-explicit escape
  hatch, unchanged by design.
- `_remove_transaction_packages` validation runs on the *summarized* removal set; the
  to-remove cascade in updates.py (596-676) already sweeps dependents, so legit plans pass.

